      "finding": "GDP deceleration to +0.5% annualized in Q4 2025 after a strong +4.4% in Q3 2025 signals potential macro softness, but BWXT's government-contracted revenue base insulates it from cyclical demand shocks.",
      "evidence": "[Source: FRED gdp_growth] — government-directed nuclear programs are largely non-discretionary and multi-year contracted."
